# cleanup-reason: the closed list of reasons a cleanup is refused. The Go core (core/teardown, safety.go) prints one as reason=<value>.
# value<TAB>mark (initial, final or -)<TAB>meaning
unreadable-copy	-	git cannot read the copy's index or history
uncommitted	-	the copy holds uncommitted changes
unmerged-local	-	a local lane holds commits that no branch of the project has
no-default-branch	-	the project's default branch cannot be determined
not-on-trunk	-	a local-trunk lane's head is not on the local trunk
no-merge-proof	-	the forge does not prove the merge
empty-lane	-	the copy never left its starting commit and its ticket is still open
check-failed	-	the safety check itself could not run
